<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA SIX-MONTH T-BILL YIELD SOARS TO 54.99 PCT.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA SIX-MONTH T-BILL YIELD SOARS TO 54.99 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield of Romanian six- month treasury bills rose to an annual 54.99 percent at Tuesday's auction from 44.01 percent last week, central bank (BNR) data showed.</p>
<p>The finance ministry's offer was oversubscribed by bids entered by 10 participants. The discount T-bills have 10 million lei face value and were placed through a single price auction by the BNR.</p>
<p>Traders said yields might ease at Wednesday's auction when the ministry offers about 300 billion lei in six-month paper.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>    Total on offer		659.03  billion lei</p>
<p>    Total bids received	 761.518 billion lei</p>
<p>    Total accepted bids	 659.034 billion lei</p>
<p>    Minimum price			  75.2278 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price			  86.8303 pct</p>
<p>    Accepted price			 78.2459 pct</p>
<p>    Annual yield			   54.99   pct</p>
<p>    Discount				 43.03   pct</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  12 Feb 1998 (182 days)</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
